StandardsMap is a plant map of the water system: each zone (generation, storage and distribution, pure steam, controls and data, fabrication, qualification) is a hairline-framed area labelled with the standards that govern it, and every code jumps to the row further down the page that proves it.

- Data: block `"type": "standards-map"` with `zones: [{t, codes, to, spot, icon}]`. `to` is the id of the section holding the proof (give that block an `anchor`, or use its nav id `s-N-label`); the zone title jumps there. `codes` are strings as the rows write them ("USP <645>", "EU GMP Annex 1"); a code may be `{t, to}` to point at another section. `spot` is a Spot or Icon name, the zone's figure (generation `ro-membrane`, storage and distribution `tank`, pure steam `pure-steam`, controls and data `cpu`, fabrication `weld`, qualification `binder`); all or none. Without spots, `icon` is an Icon name, used only when every zone has one (otherwise the `01` index).
- Markup (`blocks/standardsmap.js`): with spots, `wPlate(…, {cls:"aq-standards-map__plate"})` around `.aq-standards-map.aq-standards-map--spots`; each zone then starts with `span.aq-standards-map__fig` (aria-hidden, Spot `aq-standards-map__spot`) before `.aq-standards-map__label`. Otherwise `.aq-standards-map` > `ol.aq-standards-map__zones` (grid; `::before` is the pipe, `::after` its arrow) > `li.aq-standards-map__zone.is-up|is-down` > `.aq-standards-map__label` > `.aq-standards-map__head` (Icon `aq-standards-map__icon` or `aq-index`, `h3.aq-standards-map__t` with the section link) and `ul.aq-standards-map__codes` of `a.aq-standards-map__code` (`data-smap-code`, `data-smap-to`).
- Jump: a code chip scrolls to the row naming it (EvidenceMap rows matched on their title, spec and table rows cell by cell, whole-code match so "Annex 1" never lands on "Annex 15"), first in the zone's section, then anywhere on the page. A folded row is unfolded first; the row takes focus and flashes a `flow` outline once (`.aq-standards-map-hit`, no animation under reduced motion).
- With spots: the map sits on a plate (`line` frame on `surface-raised`); each zone is the same `line`-framed area with its 128 px vignette in `ink-muted` (`flow` on hover) beside the name (Geist 500 18/26, sentence case) and its codes. No drawing grid, corner marks or dashed leaders. Phones: the vignette (96 px) floats at each zone's right, name and code tags running beside and under it.
- Desktop: the first half of the zones above a 1 px `flow` main (the water path, a small arrow at the end), the rest below, each zone a 1 px `line` frame with a 1 px `flow` branch and a small node to the main. Codes are standard tags: Geist Mono 13/22 pills (`radius-pill`) in a 1 px `line-strong` frame with a quiet ↓, `flow` on hover. Without spots each zone leads with its Icon (`ink-muted`) or the shared index. Phones: zones stacked as compact rows on a vertical `flow` line at the left, codes wrap as tags at 12 px with a 44 px hit area.
- Ground: the section's `surface` (with spots, the plate's `surface-raised`), in either theme. Use only standards the page already lists, each pointing at a row that exists; three to six zones.
- When not to use it: a page citing fewer than about eight standards (a StandardsGrid or the rows themselves say it), or standards with no rows to prove them on the same page.

## Motion

`motion.js`: the plant is piped up in flow order. The main header draws left to right (top to bottom on phones); as it passes each zone a node seats, the branch grows out, the zone's dashed area opens from the pipe side, its vignette prints in, the leader runs to the name, the name lands and the code chips follow; the arrow lights last (about 3 s). Pipe, branches, nodes and leaders are pseudo-elements drawn through `--aq-pipe`, `--aq-arrow`, `--aq-branch`, `--aq-node`, `--aq-lead` (scale and opacity only; unset they are 1, so the map is whole without JS). Chips give a 1 px press.
